Ezero runtime source status

Original Zero runtime: tagged numbers/text/lists/phrases, 64 function frames,
copying garbage collection, one-based indexing, UTF-8 scalar size and explicit
source-line errors. The 2 MiB owned arena and exactly 64 declared variables,
including the eight prefix variables, remain the integration contract.

The file extension implements opcodes through 40, calling native adapters or
the Zero OS kernel file service. Listing results are validated, staged outside
the heap and copied into managed immutable text lists after exact allocation
reservation. No shell or external language runtime implements these operations.

Current runtime source is 41399 bytes, below the 65535-byte bundle limit.
Current verification is recorded in tests/files-verification.ztext. Historical
runtime/bytecode tests predate this extension; guest VM verification is separate.
